{visual: add title id:main_title content:"StatQuest..." duration:persist style:"font-weight: bold; font-size: large; color: black; text-align: center; position: center of the screen"}
StatQuest...
{visual: update title id:main_title content:"StatQuest...\n...is the best!!"}
...is the best!!
{visual: update title id:main_title content:"If you don't think so..."}
If you don't think so...
{visual: update title id:main_title content:"If you don't think so...\n...then we have different opinions!!!"}
...then we have different opinions!!!
{visual: update title id:main_title content:"StatQuest:\nPrincipal Component\nAnalysis (PCA) concepts in 5\nminutes!"}
Hello, I'm Josh Starmer and welcome to StatQuest. Today we're going to be talking about the main ideas behind principal component analysis, and we're going to cover those concepts in 5 minutes.
If you want more details than you get here, be sure to check out my other PCA video.
{visual: clear}
{visual: add diagram id:cells content:"A cluster of 16 circles packed together in a blob shape in the center of the screen. All 16 circles are colored green with a black outline." description:"Normal cells" duration:persist style:"position: dead center of the screen"}
{visual: add text id:caption content:"Let's say we had some normal cells..." duration:persist style:"position: directly below the cells diagram"}
Let's say we had some normal cells...
{visual: add text id:psst content:"(psst - if you're not a biologist, these could be people, or cars, or cities, etc...)" duration:temporary style:"font-size: small; position: at the very bottom edge of the screen"}
(psst - if you're not a biologist, imagine that these could be people, or cars, or cities, or etc. They could be anything.)
{visual: update text id:caption content:"Even though they look the same, we suspect that there are differences..."}
Even though they look the same, we suspect that there are differences...
{visual: update diagram id:cells content:"A cluster of 16 circles packed together. 5 circles on the left side are colored teal, while the remaining 11 circles are green. All have black outlines." description:"Teal cells"}
{visual: add highlight id:highlight1 content:"Highlighting the teal cells by giving them a thick bright yellow border." duration:persist style:"position: on the left side of the cell cluster"}
{visual: add text id:pointer_text1 content:"These might be one type of cell..." duration:persist style:"position: to the left of the teal cells"}
These might be one type of cell...
{visual: add text id:psst2 content:"(or one type of person, or car, or city, etc...)" duration:temporary style:"font-size: small; position: at the very bottom edge of the screen"}
(or one type of person, or car, or city, etc...)
{visual: update diagram id:cells content:"A cluster of 16 circles packed together. 5 on the left are teal, 3 on the top right are colored red, and the remaining 8 are green." description:"Red cells"}
{visual: add highlight id:highlight2 content:"Highlighting the red cells by giving them a thick bright yellow border." duration:persist style:"position: on the top right of the cell cluster"}
{visual: add text id:pointer_text2 content:"These might be another type of cell..." duration:persist style:"position: to the top right of the red cells"}
These might be another type of cell...
{visual: update diagram id:cells content:"A cluster of 16 circles packed together. 5 on the left are teal, 3 on the top right are red, 5 on the bottom are colored yellow, and the remaining 3 in the middle are green." description:"Yellow cells"}
{visual: add highlight id:highlight3 content:"Highlighting the yellow cells by giving them a thick bright cyan border." duration:persist style:"position: on the bottom of the cell cluster"}
{visual: add text id:pointer_text3 content:"These might be a third type of cell..." duration:persist style:"position: to the bottom right of the yellow cells"}
And lastly, these might be a third type of cell.
{visual: clear}
{visual: add diagram id:cells content:"A cluster of 16 circles packed together in a blob shape in the center. All 16 circles are colored green with a black outline." description:"Cells return to green" duration:persist style:"position: dead center of the screen"}
{visual: add text id:caption content:"Unfortunately, we can't observe the differences from the outside..." duration:persist style:"position: directly below the cells diagram"}
Unfortunately, we can't observe the differences from the outside...
{visual: update text id:caption content:"...so we sequence the mRNA in each cell to identify which genes are active. This tells us what the cell is doing."}
...so we sequence the messenger RNA in each cell to identify which genes are active. This tells us what the cell is doing.
{visual: add text id:psst3 content:"(If they were people, we could measure their height, blood pressure, reading level etc...)" duration:temporary style:"font-size: small; position: above the caption"}
(If they were people, we could measure their weight, blood pressure, reading level, etc...)
{visual: clear}
{visual: add text id:caption content:"Here's the data..." duration:persist style:"position: middle left of the screen"}
Okay, here's the data...
{visual: add table id:data_table content:"A table with 5 columns and 10 rows. Header row: empty, Cell1, Cell2, Cell3, Cell4, '...'. Row 1: Gene1, 3, 0.25, 2.8, 0.1, '...'. Row 2: Gene2, 2.9, 0.8, 2.2, 1.8, '...'. Row 3: Gene3, 2.2, 1, 1.5, 3.2, '...'. Row 4: Gene4, 2, 1.4, 2, 0.3, '...'. Row 5: Gene5, 1.3, 1.6, 1.6, 0, '...'. Row 6: Gene6, 1.5, 2.1, 2.1, 3, '...'. Row 7: Gene7, 1.1, 2.2, 1.2, 2.8, '...'. Row 8: Gene8, 1, 2.7, 0.9, 0.3, '...'. Row 9: Gene9, 0.4, 3, 0.6, 0.1, '...'. Header is light blue, Gene column is dark blue with white text, data cells are light blue." description:"Gene expression table" duration:persist style:"position: centered on the right side of the screen"}
{visual: update text id:caption content:"Each column shows how much each gene is transcribed in each cell." style:"position: centered near the top of the screen"}
Each column shows how much each gene is transcribed in each cell.
{visual: add highlight id:box1 content:"Highlighting the entire Cell1 column by changing its background color to light red." duration:temporary style:"position: on the second column of the table"}
{visual: add highlight id:box2 content:"Highlighting the entire Cell3 column by changing its background color to light red." duration:temporary style:"position: on the fourth column of the table"}
{visual: update text id:caption content:"For now, let's imagine there were only 2 cells."}
For now, let's imagine there are only two cells.
{visual: update table id:data_table content:"A table with 3 columns and 10 rows. Header row: empty, Cell1, Cell2. Row 1: Gene1, 3, 0.25. Row 2: Gene2, 2.9, 0.8. Row 3: Gene3, 2.2, 1. Row 4: Gene4, 2, 1.4. Row 5: Gene5, 1.3, 1.6. Row 6: Gene6, 1.5, 2.1. Row 7: Gene7, 1.1, 2.2. Row 8: Gene8, 1, 2.7. Row 9: Gene9, 0.4, 3." description:"Gene expression table for 2 cells"}
{visual: update text id:caption content:"We we just have 2 cells, we can plot the measurements for each gene." style:"position: top left"}
If we just have two cells, then we can plot the measurements for each gene.
{visual: add diagram id:plot content:"A 2D scatter plot. The x-axis is a horizontal black line labeled 'Cell2'. The y-axis is a vertical black line labeled 'Cell1'. There are tick marks on the axes. There are 9 blue dots representing the 9 genes plotted at their (Cell2, Cell1) coordinates: (0.25, 3), (0.8, 2.9), (1, 2.2), (1.4, 2), (1.6, 1.3), (2.1, 1.5), (2.2, 1.1), (2.7, 1), (3, 0.4). The dots form a downward sloping trend." description:"Scatter plot of gene expression" duration:persist style:"position: centered on the left side of the screen"}
{visual: add highlight id:highlight4 content:"Coloring the Gene1 dot bright red to highlight it." duration:persist style:"position: near the top-left of the scatter plot"}
{visual: add text id:pointer_text4 content:"This gene (Gene1) is highly transcribed in Cell1 and lowly transcribed in Cell2..." duration:persist style:"position: to the left of the scatter plot, near the top"}
This gene, Gene1, is highly transcribed in Cell1 and lowly transcribed in Cell2...
{visual: remove highlight id:highlight4}
{visual: add highlight id:highlight5 content:"Coloring the Gene9 dot bright red to highlight it." duration:persist style:"position: near the bottom-right of the scatter plot"}
{visual: add text id:pointer_text5 content:"... and this gene (Gene9) is lowly transcribed in Cell1 and highly transcribed in Cell2." duration:persist style:"position: underneath the scatter plot, near the bottom right"}
...and this gene, Gene9, is lowly transcribed in Cell1 and highly transcribed in Cell2.
